  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Modules keep code in manageable files, while exceptions let a program handle failure instead of hiding it.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CORE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "import brings a module into a program. try/except handles expected errors; catching a specific exception avoids hiding unrelated failures.\n\n",
      "font": "NimbusSans",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXAMPLE CODE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "import math\n\ntry:\n    value = int('42')\nexcept ValueError:\n    value = 0\nprint(math.sqrt(value))",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED RESULT\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "6.48074069840786",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE WALKTHROUGH\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "import math",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports functionality from a module; without it, the name is unavailable and may raise NameError.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "try:",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Marks operations that may fail; without a handler, an expected error can stop the caller.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "value = int('42')",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds the evaluated expression to a name; without the assignment, later lines cannot reuse that result.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "except ValueError:",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — This line continues the calculation or control flow; omitting it removes that step and may change later results.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "value = 0",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds the evaluated expression to a name; without the assignment, later lines cannot reuse that result.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(math.sqrt(value))",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Runs an expression; print displays a value and calls may have side effects—without the line, that action does not occur.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REMEMBER\n",
      "size": 19,
      "color": "#00897B",
      "bold": true
